"Evaluate the agent's response on the following criteria:\n\n1. Data loading and QC: Did the agent correctly load the count matrix, filter low-quality cells (mito fraction <20%, min genes >200), and report QC statistics? Award full credit if both filters are applied correctly.\n\n2. Normalization and feature selection: Did the agent normalize to 10,000 counts per cell, log-transform, and select highly variable genes (>=2000)?\n\n3. Dimensionality reduction and clustering: Did the agent run PCA (>=20 PCs), UMAP, and Leiden/Louvain clustering with an appropriate resolution?\n\n4. Cell type annotation: Did the agent annotate at least 5 major cell types (e.g., T cells, B cells, NK cells, myeloid cells, epithelial cells) using canonical markers?\n\n5. Differential expression: Did the agent perform DE analysis comparing responders vs non-responders using an appropriate test (Wilcoxon rank-sum or DESeq2 pseudobulk) and report adjusted p-values?\n\n6. Interpretation: Did the agent correctly identify immune cell subsets enriched in responders and provide a biologically coherent interpretation?"
